          "convergenceTargetId": "end"
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "code": "QUERY_RESPONSE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "2_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the shared Ask Oracle query agent for Marketing Strategy Advisor and Renewals Advisor. Answer user questions using only the available data fetched for the selected app area. Respect extracted query parameters for record limit, pagination, and renewal window. Do not invent program, account, ARR, revenue, risk, date, product, content, persona, buyer role, or identifier values beyond the available data. Never mention internal data-source labels, routing labels, node names, or implementation details in the user-facing response."
            },
            {
              "id": "2_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CONTEXT:\nChat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nUser question: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nApp context: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\nUser context: {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext}}\nSelected app mode and area: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_QUERY_CONTEXT.$output.result.appContextMode}} / {{$context.$nodes.ROUTE_QUERY_AREA.$output.result}}\nQuery parameters: {{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZE_QUERY_PARAMETERS.$output.result}}\nAvailable data: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_QUERY_CONTEXT.$output.result}}\n\nSUPPORTED APP MODES:\n- marketingStrategyAdvisor supports active programs, cross-sell accounts, renewal account/product summaries, and comparisons across those marketing areas.\n- renewalsAdvisor supports the visible Renewals Advisor app areas: Renewal Accounts, Buying Group Definition, Content and Messaging Strategy, and Programs.\n\nRENEWALS ADVISOR AREA GUIDANCE:\n- Renewal Accounts: answer questions about renewal accounts, account risk, ARR exposure, renewal dates/windows, usage level, risk classification, risk reasons, open opportunities, retention priorities, and account actions.\n- Buying Group Definition: answer questions about buyer roles, personas, stakeholders, and purchasing-decision influence for the selected target product.\n- Content and Messaging Strategy: answer questions about available content or message types, reference keys, collateral options, and which content area to launch.\n- Programs: answer questions about programs for the selected target product, program names, program health, on-track/needs-review status, tactic counts, and program launch targets.\n\nTASK:\nAnswer the user's current question directly from Available data. Use Chat history to resolve follow-up references to earlier questions or answers, but do not use Chat history as a source for facts unless the same facts are present in Available data.\nUse only the source or sources listed in selectedAreas unless the selected area is combined or renewalsAdvisorCombined.\nRespect queryParameters.limit when deciding how many records to describe, and respect queryParameters.renewalDays when describing renewal windows.\nIf the selected source has records, summarize the most relevant details and include concrete counts, names, industries, account numbers, ARR, revenue, renewal counts, risk counts, renewal dates, usage levels, risk classifications, buyer roles, personas, content names, reference keys, program names, tactic counts, health statuses, or badges only when those fields appear in the available data.\nIf the selected source has no records or lacks the fields needed to answer, say plainly that the information is not available for that supported area.\nIf the user asks for a comparison, compare only the areas or groups present in the available data.\nIf the user asks for an action, mention an existing app action only when the required identifiers are present. Marketing Strategy actions include launchProgram, launchCrossSellProduct, and launchRenewalAccount. Renewals Advisor actions include launchAccount, displayAccountsPage, addToProgram, addAccountToProgram, sendEmailToCSM, sendToSales, NavigateToPrograms, and launchContent. Do not fabricate action payload values.\n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn concise plain text. Use bullets only when they improve scanability. Do not output raw JSON or technical node names unless the user asks for implementation details.\nDo not mention internal data-source labels, routing labels, node names, workflow implementation details, or anything about where the answer data was assembled."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8753,
            "y": 9700
          },
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "enableActions": true,
              "customNotes": "Answer shared Ask Oracle questions from the selected app area's available data without exposing internal data-source or routing terms."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "code": "SUMMARY_RESPONSE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "3_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Return a short app summary contribution for the shared Ask Oracle query agent."
            },
            {
              "id": "3_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CONTEXT:\nApp context: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\nUser context: {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext}}\nApp mode: {{$context.$variables.appContextMode}}\n\nTASK:\nSummarize this query agent's role in one or two concise sentences. For Marketing Strategy Advisor, mention that it handles questions across active programs, cross-sell accounts, and renewal accounts. For Renewals Advisor, mention that it handles questions across renewal accounts, buying groups, content and messaging strategy, and programs. Do not invent current counts, revenue, ARR, dates, risks, or product names.\n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn plain text only."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8528,
            "y": 6982
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "code": "INIT_DISPLAY_RESPONSE",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Init Display Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "4_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Return only the requested output format. Do not include extra prose."
            },
            {
              "id": "4_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CONTEXT:\nApp context: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\nUser context: {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext}}\nApp mode: {{$context.$variables.appContextMode}}\n\nTASK:\nGenerate a startup display for the shared Ask Oracle query agent. The display should match the current app mode.\n\nFor marketingStrategyAdvisor, describe these three query areas:\n1. Active programs: program status, milestones, risks, and next steps.\n2. Cross-sell accounts: expansion opportunities, product alignment, account counts, and revenue opportunity.\n3. Renewal accounts: upcoming renewals, at-risk accounts, renewal dates, revenue exposure, and retention priorities.\n\nFor renewalsAdvisor, describe these four query areas:\n1. Renewal accounts: renewal accounts, account risk, ARR exposure, renewal windows, usage, and retention actions.\n2. Buying Group Definition: buyer roles, personas, stakeholders, and purchasing-decision influence.\n3. Content and Messaging Strategy: available content/message types, reference keys, and collateral options.\n4. Programs: program names, program health, on-track/needs-review status, tactic counts, and launch targets.\n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn exactly one oraInfoDisplay block using patternId messageListWidget.\nUse a short subtitle that fits the current app mode.\nDo not include hardcoded record counts, revenue, ARR, dates, program IDs, product IDs, account IDs, or implementation details."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9653,
            "y": 6982
          },
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "customNotes": "Use one messageListWidget that explains the query coverage areas for the current app mode."
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "6",
          "code": "RETRIEVE_PARENT_PRODUCT_NAME_AND_ID",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Retrieve Parent Product Name and Id",
            "sourceCode": "const appInput = $context.$app?.$OraAppContext || $context.$triggers?.REST?.$input?.OraAppContext || '';\nlet result = {\n  appContextMode: 'marketingStrategyAdvisor',\n  parentProductId: '',\n  parentProductName: '',\n  targetProductId: '',\n  targetProductName: ''\n};\ntry {\n  let appContextRaw = appInput;\n  if (typeof appContextRaw !== 'string') {\n    appContextRaw = JSON.stringify(appContextRaw || '');\n  }\n\n  let appContextStr = '';\n  const appContextMatch = appContextRaw.match(/appContext=([^\\s&]+)/);\n  if (appContextMatch) {\n    appContextStr = decodeURIComponent(appContextMatch[1]);\n  } else {\n    appContextStr = appContextRaw;\n  }\n\n  if ((appContextStr.startsWith('\"') && appContextStr.endsWith('\"')) || (appContextStr.startsWith(\"'\") && appContextStr.endsWith(\"'\"))) {\n    appContextStr = appContextStr.slice(1, -1);\n  }\n\n  let parentProductId = '';\n  let parentProductName = '';\n  let targetProductId = '';\n  let targetProductName = '';\n\n  const cleanValue = value => String(value || '').trim().replace(/^['\"]|['\"]$/g, '').replace(/\\+/g, ' ');\n  const assignPair = (key, value) => {\n    const normalizedKey = String(key || '').trim().replace(/^['\"]|['\"]$/g, '');\n    const normalizedValue = cleanValue(value);\n    if (normalizedKey === 'parentProductId') {\n      parentProductId = normalizedValue || parentProductId;\n    } else if (normalizedKey === 'parentProductName') {\n      parentProductName = normalizedValue || parentProductName;\n    } else if (normalizedKey === 'targetProductId') {\n      targetProductId = normalizedValue || targetProductId;\n    } else if (normalizedKey === 'targetProductName') {\n      targetProductName = normalizedValue || targetProductName;\n    }\n  };\n\n  if (appContextStr.startsWith('{') && appContextStr.endsWith('}')) {\n    try {\n      const obj = JSON.parse(appContextStr);\n      parentProductId = cleanValue(obj.parentProductId);\n      parentProductName = cleanValue(obj.parentProductName);\n      targetProductId = cleanValue(obj.targetProductId);\n      targetProductName = cleanValue(obj.targetProductName);\n    } catch (jsonError) {\n      appContextStr.slice(1, -1).split(',').forEach(pair => {\n        const separator = pair.includes('=') ? '=' : ':';\n        const parts = pair.split(separator);\n        assignPair(parts[0], parts.slice(1).join(separator));\n      });\n    }\n  } else {\n    appContextStr.split(/[,&]/).forEach(pair => {\n      const separator = pair.includes('=') ? '=' : ':';\n      const parts = pair.split(separator);\n      assignPair(parts[0], parts.slice(1).join(separator));\n    });\n  }\n\n  const appContextMode = targetProductId && !parentProductId ? 'renewalsAdvisor' : 'marketingStrategyAdvisor';\n  result = { appContextMode, parentProductId, parentProductName, targetProductId, targetProductName };\n} catch (error) {\n  result = {\n    appContextMode: 'marketingStrategyAdvisor',\n    parentProductId: '',\n    parentProductName: '',\n    targetProductId: '',\n    targetProductName: ''\n  };\n}\nreturn result;",
            "returnType": "object"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "7"
          },
          "inputs": [],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8940.5,
            "y": 5206
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "id": "7",
          "code": "SET_VARIABLES",
          "type": "SET_FIELDS",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Variables"
          },
          "outcomes": {
