        {
          "id": "1780983852384",
          "code": "EXTRACT_QUERY_PARAMETERS",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Query Parameters"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1782122075518"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1780983852384_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You extract numeric query parameters for the shared Marketing Strategy Advisor and Renewals Advisor query workflow. Return only the structured fields requested by the output schema. Do not answer the user question."
            },
            {
              "id": "1780983852384_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "CONTEXT:\nChat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nUser question: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nAction payload: {{$context.$app.$OraAction}}\nApp context: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\nUser context: {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext}}\n\nTASK:\nDetermine the Business Object query parameters requested by the user. Use Chat history only to resolve contextual follow-up wording in the current question, such as references to the same area, previous result, first item, or prior renewal window.\n\nDefaults when the user does not explicitly request a value:\n- limit: 10\n- pageLimit: 10\n- pageOffset: 0\n- renewalDays: 180\n\nRules:\n- limit is the total number of records requested by the user. pageLimit is the preferred page size, but account display pagination is normalized later to the workflow page-size variable.\n- Set limit/pageLimit only when the current question or its follow-up context asks for a number of records, rows, items, results, accounts, programs, products, opportunities, or renewals. Examples: \"limit 10\", \"limit set to 10\", \"show 20 renewal accounts\", \"first 7 records\".\n- Do not treat analytical ranking requests like \"top 3 industries\" as a record limit unless the user asks for records/accounts/results.\n- pageOffset should be 0 by default. If the user says \"offset N\", \"starting at N\", or \"skip N\", set pageOffset to N.\n- renewalDays should be 180 by default. Convert weeks to days using 7 days per week, months to days using 30 days per month, and years to days using 365 days per year. Examples: \"next 2 weeks\" -> 14, \"within 6 months\" -> 180, \"next 1 year\" -> 365, \"renewal days set to 90\" -> 90.\n- Keep numeric values as integers.\n- Clamp limit/pageLimit between 1 and 100. Clamp pageOffset between 0 and 10000. Clamp renewalDays between 1 and 365.\n- hasExplicitLimit is true only when the user explicitly asked for a record count or limit.\n- hasExplicitRenewalDays is true only when the user explicitly asked for a renewal window.\n- matchedLimitText and matchedRenewalDaysText should contain the short phrase from the user that caused the value, or an empty string when defaulted.\n\nOUTPUT:\nReturn only the structured output fields defined by the schema."
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8978,
            "y": 7204
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"limit\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"pageLimit\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"pageOffset\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"renewalDays\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"hasExplicitLimit\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"hasExplicitRenewalDays\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"matchedLimitText\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"matchedRenewalDaysText\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"limit\",\n    \"pageLimit\",\n    \"pageOffset\",\n    \"renewalDays\",\n    \"hasExplicitLimit\",\n    \"hasExplicitRenewalDays\",\n    \"matchedLimitText\",\n    \"matchedRenewalDaysText\"\n  ]\n}\n"
        },
